extends layout

block content
  .col-md-12.cardSpacer
    #page-header-container(style='align-items:flex-start')
      #page-title-container
        h3#page-title Privacy Policy
        .sub-page-header.text-muted Public blockchain data, server logs, advertising, and user safety.
      .cardSpacer.clearfix

    .card.card-default.border-0.cardSpacer
      .card-header
        strong Public blockchain data
      .card-body
        p.lead.mb-3 SumExplorer displays information that already exists on the public Sumcoin blockchain.
        p.mb-0 This may include block hashes, transaction IDs, public addresses, timestamps, amounts, confirmations, block heights, rich list entries, and network statistics. Public blockchain data can be viewed and analyzed by anyone.

    .row
      .col-md-6.cardSpacer
        .card.card-default.border-0.h-100
          .card-header
            strong Site usage information
          .card-body
            p Standard web server logs may include request details such as IP address, browser type, requested URL, referring page, and timestamp.
            p.mb-0 This information is used for security, abuse prevention, troubleshooting, uptime monitoring, and improving site reliability.
      .col-md-6.cardSpacer
        .card.card-default.border-0.h-100
          .card-header
            strong Advertising and third parties
          .card-body
            p SumExplorer may use third-party services such as content delivery networks, analytics tools, or advertising networks.
            p.mb-0 These services may process basic browser, device, or request information according to their own privacy policies.

    .card.card-default.border-0.cardSpacer
      .card-header
        strong Wallet privacy reminder
      .card-body
        ul.mb-0
          li Do not enter private keys, seed words, or wallet passwords into a block explorer.
          li Public addresses are visible on-chain and may be analyzed by third parties.
          li Avoid publishing personal information that connects your identity to a public blockchain address unless you intend to do so.
          li SumExplorer cannot remove confirmed public blockchain history.
